A note on what this does and does not do: this is a static web app, so its code
is readable by anyone who opens the page, and no licence changes that. What the
terms above give you is a legal position if somebody republishes the work as
their own, not a technical barrier against it.

Trouble code descriptions are the generic SAE definitions and are not
copyrightable as facts. The repair guidance, the interface, the artwork and the
code are.
